    "_comment": "CHAMPIONSHIP CHAPTER TEMPLATE — 100-round worked example. Files here named chXXXXX.json load at startup (restart to pick up new ones; _-prefixed files like this one are ignored by the loader — copy to e.g. ch00001.json to make it creatable). Create in-game with: cd-createchampionship template <name>. Full authoring guide: docs/championship-guide.md.",
    "_fields": "name = unique championship name. duration = days (number or \"14d\") or \"unlimited\" — the timer starts at cd-startchampionship, NOT at create. isVIP = optional bool. roster = 1-100 rounds in play order.",
    "_round_fields": "carID + upgrade (000/333/666/699/969/996) + track are required per round. _round is a LABEL for your own navigation — it is ignored at create time, as is any other _-prefixed or unknown key. reqs = optional hand requirements, same shapes as cd-filter. rewards = optional, MAX 3 types: money/fuseTokens/trophies (numbers), car ({carID, upgrade}), pack (packID), driver (driverID).",
    "_verify": "node scripts/checkChampionship.js src/championships/<file>.json — proves every round is well-formed AND beatable by at least one car in the game.",
